# JSON Gateway - manual test requests
#
# Works with the IntelliJ HTTP Client (click ▶ next to a request) and the VS Code
# "REST Client" extension (click "Send Request").
#
# Start the app first:   make run        (PostgreSQL + WireMock via docker compose, demo flows)
#                   or:  make run-test   (throwaway DB, no compose)
#
# Each request says what to expect. The demo downstream data comes from
# src/test/resources/wiremock/mappings/core-banking.json:
#   1001 BUDI SANTOSO  active, has history     2002 SITI AMINAH  active, no history
#   3003 ANDI WIJAYA   blocked                 9999 not found (core code 14)
#   7777 slow (8 s)                            amount 999999999 -> core code 51 (insufficient funds)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminToken = dev-admin-token

###############################################################################
# Operations
###############################################################################

### Health - expect 200 {"status":"UP"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Hikari pool metrics - expect 200, tag pool=gateway-pool
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics/hikaricp.connections.active

### Reload configuration from the DB - expect 200 {"flows":8,"loadedAt":"..."} (3 demo flows + 5 tbl_ms_user CRUD flows; 9 once the tutorial flow is loaded)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/config/reload
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

### Reload with a wrong token - expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/config/reload
X-Admin-Token: wrong-token

###############################################################################
# Flow ACCOUNT_INQUIRY: GET /v1/accounts/{accountNo}
# single step, lookup (statusCd A -> ACTIVE), converter TO_NUMBER, default currency
###############################################################################

### Account inquiry - expect 200
# {"accountNo":"1001","accountName":"BUDI SANTOSO","balance":1500000.00,"currency":"IDR","status":"ACTIVE"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/1001

### Account without currency from core - expect 200, "currency":"IDR" (default_value)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/2002

### Blocked account - expect 200, "status":"BLOCKED"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/3003

### Channel header forwarded to core - expect 200 (core receives X-Channel: ATM instead of default MOBILE)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/1001
X-Channel: ATM

### Own correlation ID - expect 200 and response header X-Correlation-Id: my-trace-001
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/1001
X-Correlation-Id: my-trace-001

### Unknown account - expect 404 {"errorCode":"ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND",...} (core 404 + code 14, mapped by coreBankingErrorHandler)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/9999

### Slow downstream - expect 504 {"errorCode":"GW-504-DOWNSTREAM",...} after ~5 s (dev read timeout)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/7777

###############################################################################
# Flow ACCOUNT_HISTORY: GET /v1/accounts/{accountNo}/transactions
# array mapping items[*] -> transactions[*], DATE_FORMAT, lookup D/C -> DEBIT/CREDIT, query default
###############################################################################

### History with default limit (core called with ?limit=10) - expect 200
# {"accountNo":"1001","transactions":[{"date":"2026-10-01","amount":150000.00,"type":"CREDIT"},
#                                     {"date":"2026-10-03","amount":25000.50,"type":"DEBIT"}]}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/1001/transactions

### History with explicit limit (core called with ?limit=5) - expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/1001/transactions?limit=5

###############################################################################
# Flow TRANSFER: POST /v1/transfers
# request schema, parallel lookups (source + beneficiary), conditional debit,
# success_expr on responseCode, CONTINUE notification, error mapping
###############################################################################

### Successful transfer - expect 200
# {"transactionId":"TRX20261008001","status":"SUCCESS","beneficiaryName":"SITI AMINAH","notification":"SUCCESS"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "1001",
  "toAccount": "2002",
  "amount": 1000,
  "note": "Lunch"
}

### Insufficient funds - expect 422 {"errorCode":"INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS","errorMessage":"Insufficient balance",...}
# core answers HTTP 200 with responseCode 51 -> success_expr false -> lookup CORE_BANKING_ERRORS
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "1001",
  "toAccount": "2002",
  "amount": 999999999
}

### Blocked beneficiary - expect 200, debit skipped by condition_expr
# {"status":"SKIPPED","beneficiaryName":"ANDI WIJAYA","notification":"SUCCESS"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "1001",
  "toAccount": "3003",
  "amount": 1000
}

### Unknown beneficiary - expect 404 {"errorCode":"ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND",...} (lookup step fails, STOP)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "1001",
  "toAccount": "9999",
  "amount": 1000
}

### Schema violation - expect 400 {"errorCode":"GW-400-SCHEMA","details":["$: required property 'toAccount' not found", ...]}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "1001",
  "amount": -5
}

### Sensitive field - expect 200; in the audit table the pin is stored as "****" (make audit / gw_audit_transaction)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: masking-check-001

{
  "fromAccount": "1001",
  "toAccount": "2002",
  "amount": 1000,
  "pin": "123456"
}

### Body is not JSON - expect 400 {"errorCode":"GW-400-JSON",...}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ this is not json

###############################################################################
# Routing
###############################################################################

### No flow for this method + path - expect 404 {"errorCode":"GW-404-ROUTE",...}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/1001

### Unknown path - expect 404 {"errorCode":"GW-404-ROUTE",...}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/does-not-exist

###############################################################################
# Tutorial flow ACCOUNT_OVERVIEW (docs/CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md)
# Only exists after loading docs/examples/account-overview.sql and reloading:
#   docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U gateway -d gateway < docs/examples/account-overview.sql
#   make reload
###############################################################################

### Account overview - expect 200 and response header X-Data-Source: CORE_BANKING
# {"account":{"number":"1001","holder":"BUDI SANTOSO","status":"ACTIVE","balance":1500000.00},
#  "recent":[{"date":"01/10/2026",...},...],"historyStatus":"SUCCESS","requestedBy":"teller-07"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/accounts/1001/overview
X-User-Id: teller-07

### Account overview, history unavailable - expect 200 with "historyStatus":"FAILED" and no "recent" (CONTINUE step)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/accounts/2002/overview

###############################################################################
# Custom class examples, flow PARTNER_ACCOUNT_INQUIRY (docs/CUSTOM-CLASSES.md)
# Only exists after loading docs/examples/custom-classes.sql and reloading:
#   docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U gateway -d gateway < docs/examples/custom-classes.sql
#   make reload
###############################################################################

### channelGuard: no X-Channel - expect 403 {"errorCode":"CHANNEL_NOT_ALLOWED","errorMessage":"X-Channel header is required",...}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v3/accounts/1001

### channelGuard: unknown channel - expect 403 "Channel 'TELLER' is not allowed"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v3/accounts/1001
X-Channel: TELLER

### Allowed channel - expect 200, balance via idrAmountFormatter; core receives X-Timestamp + X-Signature (requestSigner)
# {"responseCode":"00","responseMessage":"Approved","accountNo":"1001","accountName":"BUDI SANTOSO","balance":"Rp1.500.000,00"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v3/accounts/1001
X-Channel: MOBILE

### partnerErrorHandler: unknown account - expect HTTP 200 {"responseCode":"14","responseMessage":"Account not found",...}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v3/accounts/9999
X-Channel: ATM

### partnerErrorHandler: timeout - expect HTTP 200 {"responseCode":"68","responseMessage":"Response received too late",...} after ~5 s
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v3/accounts/7777
X-Channel: WEB

###############################################################################
# tbl_ms_user CRUD (custom table, MsUserHandlers; flows in 102-dev-demo-ms-user.xml)
###############################################################################

### Create (POST) - expect 201 + Location: /api/v1/users/{id}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"rina.k","fullName":"Rina Kartika","email":"rina@example.com","phone":"+6281234567","status":"ACTIVE"}

### Create with a taken username - expect 409 USERNAME_TAKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"budi.santoso","fullName":"Another Budi"}

### Create without fullName - expect 400 GW-400-SCHEMA
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"no.name"}

### List (GET) - expect 200 {"content":[...],"page":1,"size":10,"totalElements":...,"totalPages":...}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users

### List page 2 of 2 per page, active only, searching "a" - expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?page=2&size=2&status=ACTIVE&search=a

### List with bad paging - expect 400 INVALID_QUERY
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?page=0&size=500

### Detail (GET) - expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/1

### Detail of a missing user - expect 404 USER_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/999999

### Update (PUT) - expect 200 with the new values
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName":"Budi Santoso, S.E.","phone":"081299999999"}

### Update the username - expect 400 (not allowed by MS_USER_UPDATE_REQUEST)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"budi"}

### Delete (DELETE) - expect 204 (run "Create" first and use its id)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/4

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Database query steps (103-dev-demo-sql-flows.xml): SQL on GATEWAY_DB, parameters from the request
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### One user: :id <- path id (TO_NUMBER); no row -> 422 GW-422-BUSINESS
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sql/users/1

### Search: :q, :status (UPPER), :limit (TO_NUMBER, default 10) <- query string
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sql/users?q=budi&status=active&limit=5

### Values are bound, not pasted into the SQL: this finds nothing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sql/users?q=%27%20OR%20%271%27%3D%271

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### File uploads (104-dev-demo-file-flows.xml): stored in LOCAL_FILES (./data/files)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Multipart: field "file" (required) + "description"; returns fileId (the key)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=gw

--gw
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Invoice October
--gw
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="invoice.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Total: 150000
--gw--

### Raw body: the whole body is the file; its name from X-File-Name
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/documents
Content-Type: application/octet-stream
X-File-Name: notes.txt

hello from a raw upload

### Delete: the fileId of an upload, e.g. 2026/10/<uuid>-invoice.txt
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files/2026/10/replace-with-uuid-invoice.txt
